yeah here you go, we now have 60fps celeste on picotron. this is (probably) usable as a base cart for modding, i've kept stuff as modular as possible.

based on:
- original celeste classic as a reference
- evercore for the implementations of a lot of mechanics
- evertron for picotron code style inspiration

which were made by the following very cool people:
- maddy thorson
- noel berry
- petra
- meep
- gonengazit
- akliant
- ooooggll
- pancelor

also thank you to these people for playtesting:
- sheebeehs
- wisper (superboi0119)
- aurora

differences from the original celeste classic:
- hair physics are completely different
- camera is also completely different
- it's 60fps (no shit)
- the codebase is very differently structured
- i forgot the rest, if you have the time make a PR to document the other differences

other than that, the codebase is probably decently readable and well-commented enough for you to know what you're doing, have fun!

